According to the IEEE, a Requirement is
 A condition or capability needed by a user to solve a problem or achieve an objective
 A condition or capability that must be met or possessed by a system or system component to satisfy a contract, standard, specification, or other formally imposed document
 A documented representation of a condition or capability as in answer 1 or 2
 All the above (tick)

Which of the following is NOT a System Requirement type?
 Non-functional Requirement

The System Requirement Life Cycle Process starts with which activity?
 Analyzing Stakeholder Requirements

From which Polarion project Topic can a user import a Word Document?
 Documents and Pages

When exporting a LiveDoc for external collaboration, which export options are available in Polarion?
 Review, Collaboration, & Prioritization

