Which of the following is NOT an approach to increase capacity, speed, and quality?
 Round-Trip Approach

Which statement best defines the cloning approach?
 We have a copy of the element, and the products themselves stay highly independent as nothing from the design should flow between them

Which statement best defines the reuse of common elements (core assets)?
 Core assets are maintained and managed in a portfolio of features and then reused in different variants of your products

When branching a document, what happens to the work items contained in the document?
 They are inserted as referenced work items

Which of these is true about referenced work items?
 Referenced work items can be frozen so that no modifications are propagated to them, and can be unfrozen if needed.

Which statement best defines the Polarion merging capability?
 The merging capability allows changes from the work items to flow from the child document back to the master

Which two Polarion features both result in a new document being created?
 Branching, Combining
